  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nMarked price (M.P) = 125% × cost price (C.P)\n\n**Formula used:**\n\nC.P/M.P = (100 - D%)/(100 ± P/L%)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\nC.P : M.P = 125 : 100 = 5 : 4\n\n⇒ C.P/M.P = (100 - D%)/(100 + P%)\n\n⇒ 4/5 = 90/(100 + P%)\n\n⇒ (100 + P%) = (90 × 5)/4\n\n⇒ (100 + P%) = 450/4\n\n⇒ (100 + P%) = 112.5\n\n⇒ P% = (112.5 - 100) = 12.5\n\n**∴ The correct answer is 12(1)/(2)\\%.**\n\n** [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/c76c13ba2d2ab46b47f8a931ae621dac081a0cb266b142dc23f58659fac4a466.png] __Alternate Method__**Calculation:\n\nDiscount% = M.P : S.P = 10 : 9 ------ (1) \n\nM.P : C.P = 125 : 100 = (5 : 4) × 2\n\nM.P : C.P = 10 : 8 ------- (2)\n\nFrom eq. (1) & (2)\n\nC.P : M.P : S.P = 8 : 10 : 9\n\nGain % = {(9 - 8) × 100}/8\n\n⇒ 100/8 = 12(1)/(2)\\% \n\n∴ The correct answer is 12(1)/(2)\\%.",
